      "problem": "Express $2{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{5})-1$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n2{cos}^{2}⁡x-1=\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{4\\pi }{5}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{cos}^{2}⁡(\\frac{4\\pi }{5})-1 & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{4\\pi }{5}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{8\\pi }{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
